	<p style="text-align: justify;" class="indent"> &nbsp; &nbsp;My elders are natives of the cities of Multan and Kasoor from pre-1947 British India, which today forms a part of the Islamic State of Pakistan. Multan, where the origins of my father's side lie, hosts the Prahalad Puri temple. The city was conquered nearly within a century of the advent of Islam. Mr. A. I. Kolesnikov states in UNESCO's 'History of Civilisations of Central Asia' in relation to treatment of conquered subjects like them (Iskender-Mochiri & Kolesnikov, 1996, Pg. 462): </p>

	<p style="text-align: justify;">- "People of ‘other religions’ who signed a treaty with the Muslims became dhimmmīs (ahl al-dhimma), or people who enjoyed the protection of the Muslim community. Although Zoroastrians, Christians and Jews were not always accorded the same treatment, the conditions of the treaties did not vary greatly according to the religion of the subjugated group."</p>
	
	<p style="text-align: justify;" class="indent">&nbsp; &nbsp;My faith is Sanatana Dharma, the oldest practiced faith in the world. To understand it, requires training. The crude iconoclast invading hordes operating with fanatic zeal, seeking to enslave and usurp property and land, had little intention to understand the sophisticated places of worship holding multiple dieties from a non-Abrahamic faith. Hence, <B><a href="./misconceptions.php">'Kāfir'</a></B> is the term my community got, and hence the terms of peace were "unimaginable" in today's context. My ancestors would have hence resisted. As per Kolesnikov, this led to ethnic cleansing: </p>

	<p style="text-align: justify;">- "If an area was subjugated ‘by force of arms’, part of the population was put to death or enslaved; those who escaped such a fate were constrained to pay heavy taxes, or were forced to emigrate, or had to conclude an agreement with the victors at great disadvantage to themselves (Iskender-Mochiri & Kolesnikov, 1997, Pg. 462)."</p>	
	
	<p style="text-align: justify;" class="indent">&nbsp; &nbsp;My ancestors despite at times unbelievable odds stuck around in Multan, due to our inseparable ancient temple of HIS[HER/THEIR]  HOLINESS LATE devotee Prahalad - 'The Prahalad Puri Temple' - Palace location where Śrī Śrī Bhagavān Rādhā-Kṛṣṇa took Avatar to defend the five year old devotee Prince Prahlad</p> 
	
		   <p><i id="mm1ancestors" style="text-align: center;"> Item 1: Ancestral temple</i></p>	

